research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:59:### A1 — EFT models, scales, and Wilsonian integration (`aqft-eft-foundations`)
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:61:Definitions should distinguish the microscopic model, its light fields, heavy fields/thresholds, regulator, Wilsonian scale `mu`, heavy mass/scale `M`, external energy `E`, and EFT cutoff `Lambda`; do not use those three scales interchangeably. Fix spacetime, signature, units, field spaces/representations, regularity, gauge/flavor symmetries, and normalization of the action. Define a Wilsonian action as a functional integral or rigorously specified finite-regulator pushforward over a declared high-mode sector. Define a local derivative expansion and its truncation as an asymptotic/organized approximation with named power-counting assumptions, not as a convergent series by default. Keep it distinct from a 1PI effective action and from a renormalized time-ordered product.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:67:**Missing prerequisite:** a generic interacting Wilsonian mode split needs a declared regulated measure/action and well-defined integration over high modes; a continuum version needs existence and estimates for the measure/functionals used. A generic derivative-expansion remainder needs analyticity/locality assumptions and a normed observable class with an actual remainder proof. The current Gaussian theorem covers only a positive quadratic heavy sector and band-limited source. It supplies none of these general existence claims.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:69:### A2 — Power counting, operator spaces, and redundancy (`aqft-eft-operators`)
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:81:### A3 — Matching, threshold changes, and RG flow (`aqft-eft-matching-running`)
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:83:Define a renormalization scheme, scale-dependent coefficient vector, beta function/anomalous-dimension matrix, and matching map. Matching should equate a declared set of renormalized low-energy amplitudes/Green functions in the full and effective theories at a scale near a specified threshold, with identical IR regulators and renormalization conventions; it should state loop order, operator basis, mass expansion, and finite terms. Separate matching (changing field content/threshold) from running (evolving coefficients within one EFT). For several thresholds, state the ordered composition of matching and evolution maps.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:85:Candidate items: `def-aqft-scheme-and-wilson-coefficients`; `def-aqft-threshold-matching-map`; `prop-aqft-matching-and-running-scale-independence`; `thm-aqft-truncated-coupled-rge-wellposedness`; `ex-aqft-qed-threshold-matching`; and a SUSY threshold example coordinated with the supersymmetry researcher. A one-loop SMEFT RGE coefficient is only a theorem after the basis, flavor assumptions, regulator/subtraction scheme, and computed matrix entries are explicit. The `Jenkins–Manohar–Trott` three-paper result gives one-loop dimension-six running for its assumptions; it is an external statement to reproduce or import only through the approved exact source protocol.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:89:Required result obligation: prove that, through the stated perturbative/EFT truncation, a physical prediction is unchanged by changing the intermediate renormalization scale when the coefficient running, threshold matching, and matrix elements are combined consistently. Propagate omitted loop orders and higher-dimensional operators as separate theory uncertainties; do not label scheme-independent observables as exact Wilson coefficients.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:91:### A4 — SMEFT, HEFT, and symmetry realization (`aqft-smeft-heft`)
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:99:### A5 — Amplitudes, dispersion relations, positivity, and bootstrap (`aqft-eft-amplitudes`)
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:107:### A6 — EFT gauge and anomaly interface (`aqft-eft-anomalies`)
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:111:Candidate items: `def-aqft-anomaly-matching-data`; `prop-aqft-heavy-chiral-threshold-wess-zumino-match`; and `ex-aqft-heavy-fermion-anomaly-threshold`, but only after the gauge/anomaly researcher supplies the exact local definitions, anomaly normalization, and hypotheses. Reuse `qftx-bv-brst`, `qftx-anomaly-cocycles`, and `def-qftx-chiral-anomaly-interface` at their actual Abelian/scalar or purely mathematical interfaces. `D'Hoker–Farhi` and Wess–Zumino/Witten sources are candidate literature inputs; any coefficient-level statement must identify representations, symmetry breaking, regulator, descent convention, and admissible local counterterms. The current local QFT item does not prove the general non-Abelian threshold-matching statement.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:113:### A7 — Supersymmetric EFT bridge (`aqft-susy-effective-theories`)
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:115:Use the supersymmetry researcher's exact `N=1`/other supersymmetry conventions and items. Define the allowed supersymmetric local operators in superspace, superpotential and Kähler/gauge-kinetic terms, the Wilsonian scale, and the selected UV/IR multiplets. A basis should be reduced by superspace integration by parts, superfield equations of motion, gauge identities, and allowed superfield redefinitions, with the same fixed-order amplitude/effective-action equivalence obligation as A2. Distinguish Wilsonian holomorphic data from 1PI quantities. If soft breaking is introduced, state the spurion representation and the exact power counting for soft terms; do not assume arbitrary soft breaking is a small perturbation without bounds.
research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:117:Candidate items: `def-aqft-susy-wilsonian-action`; `prop-aqft-supersymmetric-threshold-matching`; `thm-aqft-wilsonian-superpotential-nonrenormalization` (only with the regulator, field content, gauge invariance, perturbative scope, and chiral/holomorphic definitions of the selected source); and `ex-aqft-soft-breaking-effective-operator`. Weinberg's perturbative theorem is a candidate source for the nonrenormalization obligation: it allows arbitrary gauge-invariant holomorphic `F(Phi,W)` in the Wilsonian Lagrangian, apart from one-loop gauge-coupling renormalization, subject to a cutoff preserving supersymmetry and gauge invariance. It is not a claim about nonperturbative corrections, arbitrary 1PI actions, or a model-independent absence of all running. Use the physical BPS bridge only after the localization/BPS researcher establishes it; the existing mathematical CoHA contract explicitly demands an additional dictionary and proves no physical index identity.
