research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-eft-experiments.md:161:Do not mark an established EFT theorem as an `open-problem` simply because its proof is absent locally. The missing generic Wilsonian integration, operator-quotient proof, threshold matching error bounds, gauge-compatible all-order renormalization, HEFT/SMEFT full correspondence, massless/gravitational positivity extension, and model-independent supersymmetric threshold claims are authoring or scope obligations unless a precise current source/status review shows the mathematical statement is genuinely unresolved. Conversely, do not put a source-backed conjecture, formal perturbative identity, or experimental interpretation into a proved dependency without the actual hypotheses and argument.

